+<a id="turn-executor"></a>
+### External turn executor
+
+To delegate execution within the [native turn lifecycle](../../../docs/architecture.md#turn-flow), call `ctx.agentLoop.registerTurnExecutor('turn:' + stableName, { authorize, run, afterCommit, release })` from the owning Cordis fiber. `afterCommit` and `release` are optional. Each provider permits one live registration. The disposer revokes the registration, then cancels and awaits its admitted work. The callbacks are trusted Host code; the loop does not grant them the submitting client's identity or request authority.
+
+The loop fixes the execution branch and any executor route at native turn entry. `agent.model.current()` and the `modelSelection.next` projection still describe the next selection. When the current selection points to an executor during an ordinary turn, a continuation uses the last ordinary step's selection.
+
+An executor turn accepts only a `next-turn` message approved by `authorize` with a live ticket from the current registration for that exact queue occurrence. Steering is refused without removing the queued prompt. Changing mode or the turn model cannot reroute pending work. The loop never falls back to a model adapter or automatically replays executor work, including when dispatch is uncertain.
+
+The loop starts the leased job only after it atomically appends `step/start` and `user/message` and dequeues the message in memory. It calls `run` only after flushing that admission through the exact durable write handle it owns for the Session.
+
+The plugin must register its actual execution authority, filter the data it sends to the provider, and bring its processes to quiescence. It must revalidate authorization and call `assertDispatchable` immediately before each possible dispatch, with no intervening `await`. Registration does not bypass permission checks.
